media: econ-cam57: fix control errors, saturation and IR exposure initialization

Preserve the existing IR control IDs, raw units, ranges and defaults. Userspace
stages gain first and writes exposure to apply both in manual mode. Repeated
exposure writes must reach the driver so gain-only changes are not skipped.
Automatic requests must also be sent even when their cached value matches.
Register IR automatic exposure after the manual controls so control setup
finishes in automatic mode.

Return the existing control callback result instead of discarding errors.
Match saturation's advertised range to its 0..10 lookup table and use the
vendor default of 7, replacing the invalid default of 128.

Use the existing status checker to wait through RESET and ONGOING. Keep raw
firmware error statuses for flash retry decisions; translate them to negative
errors in the control mailbox sender. No IR-specific polling or delay is needed.

Leave power-line frequency control registration commented out, as in the vendor
source. The tested firmware rejects the 50 Hz default with status 0x55, aborting
control setup. Command support needs verification before exposing this control.

Keep the control handler alive across link loss so reconnection can reapply its
controls. Release it unconditionally on driver removal, including while offline.

IR units and RGB exposure commands are unchanged. Unit conversion belongs to
the userspace camera adapter. CAM31 and stream configuration are unchanged.

